# Atlas AI Rules

Canonical decision: `docs/architecture/adr-001-acting-first-eve.md`.

- Eve in `apps/agent` is the acting brain; tools call Atlas domain services only.
- Prefer soft source links (G1). Do not invent private memory facts when nothing relevant was retrieved.
- Do not productize proof/receipt/policy-hash UIs.
- Use structured outputs and validate them before writes.
- Store operator traces (prompt/model/tool metadata) for evals; not as end-user product.
- Memory writes are mostly auto (M1); only low-confidence or conflicts go to Inbox review.
- External actions use P1 risk mapping: auto for internal writes and drafts; short confirm for real external writes; Level 4 forbidden.
- No sandbox/code-mode default in MVP (S0).
- Workflow SDK for durable Eve sessions and ingestion; not Temporal by default.
- AI behavior changes require eval or smoke test updates.
- Apply `docs/architecture/privacy-redaction-policy.md` before sending retrieved chunks, prompts, screenshots, fixtures, or raw source excerpts to external providers.
- Do not let a model decide what is unnecessary or safe to disclose.
- Prefer structured facts, source IDs, derived values, and stable pseudonyms before exact raw text when the task permits it.
- Fake/local model adapters must exist for ordinary local development.
